-- title:
--   A place with j-pole fixed by the translation automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and write [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) for the $\mathbb C$-subalgebra of the algebra of all functions $\mathbb H \to \mathbb C$ generated by the function $\tau \mapsto E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$ together with the functions `fricke N v` for all nonzero $v \in (\mathbb Z/N)^2$. Let $K$ be a field carrying algebra structures over $\mathbb C$ and over this subalgebra, compatibly (scalar tower), and such that $K$ is a fraction field of the subalgebra. Assume that the subalgebra is stable under the substitution $F \mapsto (\tau \mapsto F(T^{-1}\cdot\tau))$, where $T$ is the standard translation matrix in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. Then there is a place $W$ of $K$ over $\mathbb C$, that is, a valuation subring of $K$ containing the image of $\mathbb C$, different from all of $K$, and a principal ideal ring, such that: (i) the associated normalised order function, $\operatorname{ord}_W = -\log$ of the adic valuation attached to the height-one prime of $W$, is strictly negative on the image in $K$ of the generator $E_4^3/\Delta$; and (ii) every $\mathbb C$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $K$ which sends (the image of) each $F$ in the subalgebra to (the image of) $\tau \mapsto F(T^{-1}\cdot\tau)$ fixes $W$, for the action on places of the semilinear automorphism $(\varphi, \mathrm{id}_{\mathbb C})$ attached to $\varphi$.
--
--   The place produced is the cusp $i\infty$ of the modular curve of level $N$, described through the order of vanishing in the local parameter $q_N = e^{2\pi i \tau/N}$; at it $j$ has a pole, and it is visibly invariant under the automorphism induced by $\tau \mapsto \tau+1$. It feeds the genus and degree estimates for the function field of level $N$ and the counting of fibres of the $j$-map over double cosets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_exists_place_ord_neg_forall_smul_eq.lean

